 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Clean them with a little bit of dish soap and water, and a soft brush. Rub in the direction of the bristles, never against them. That's nice of you for brush share. A few drops of water are good for them, and help keep the bristles soft. You can, sort of. You need to hit them with good dry brush first, then wash them. A little bit of dish soap helps break up enough. Then a little bit of a mild all purpose cleaner will do. Just rinse it right out immediately.",
